AIDS :
About the Department
Artificial Intelligence and Data Science (AIDS) is a branch of engineering that focuses on developing intelligent systems and analyzing vast amounts of data to derive meaningful insights. It integrates machine learning, deep learning, big data analytics, natural language processing, and cloud computing to solve complex real-world problems. AIDS engineers work on cutting-edge technologies such as AI-driven automation, predictive analytics, computer vision, and cybersecurity, driving innovation across industries like healthcare, finance, e-commerce, and smart cities. With the exponential growth of data and advancements in AI, the field continues to evolve, enhancing decision-making, efficiency, and automation. As the world moves towards an AI-powered future, Artificial Intelligence and Data Science play a crucial role in transforming industries and improving everyday life.

