CSD :
About the Department
Computer Science and Design (CSD) is a branch of engineering that blends computing technologies with design principles to create user-centric digital solutions. It integrates software development, human-computer interaction, UI/UX design, multimedia processing, and virtual reality to enhance user experience and digital innovation. CSD engineers work on cutting-edge technologies such as interactive web applications, game development, augmented reality, and creative AI, driving advancements in industries like media, entertainment, e-learning, and product design. With the growing demand for aesthetically appealing and functional digital interfaces, the field continues to evolve, bridging the gap between technology and design. As digital experiences become more immersive and intuitive, Computer Science and Design plays a vital role in shaping the future of interactive technology.

